# APP_BASE_URL is the one origin this deployment treats as its own: what binds an
# OAuth redirect, the authenticator relying-party origin, every emailed link, and
# the frontend solution proxy's same-origin judgement.
#
# It is OPERATOR configuration, and nothing in a request can establish it. A
# deployed cell that has not set it refuses those surfaces rather than resolving
# an origin some other way: accounts refuses to start without it, and the frontend
# refuses to serve sign-in or the solution proxy. Local development pins no
# runtime port, so it is empty here and the frontend uses its own discovered
# loopback endpoint, which is the host the browser reaches anyway.
#
# Since issue #1003 it is also this host's OAuth 2.1 ISSUER: the `iss` of every
# access token and the `issuer` of the RFC 8414 document published at
# <APP_BASE_URL>/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server. RFC 8414 §2 requires that
# issuer to be an https URL, so the two can only be equal if this is set — a
# client that discovers the metadata and then verifies `iss` against it refuses a
# token naming anything else. Unset (the default here) means no metadata is
# published and tokens keep the pre-metadata literal issuer, so the two cannot
# disagree. A deployment that wants an MCP client to discover it MUST set this;
# the gateway reads the same value to publish a solution's protected-resource
# metadata and to require a token's resource audience to name this host.
#
# Write it as a hostname or a dotted-quad address. A numeric spelling of an
# address (`https://2130706433`, `https://0x7f000001`, `https://127.1`) is
# REFUSED: the browser's URL parser re-renders those as the dotted quad while Go
# preserves what was written, so the two services would compare different values
# from this one line and every same-origin check would fail.
#
# DECLARED ONCE. This file carried it twice after a merge — one key under two
# spellings — and the configuration loader refuses that outright, which takes down
# every database-backed suite and the local run with it.
APP_BASE_URL=

# Interactive links use the origin above. A background-only production origin may
# be supplied by deployment configuration.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=

# Who may create an organization: `open` (empty is the same), `platform_admin`,
# or `disabled`; any other value refuses accounts' boot. Declared because
# accounts has read it from this group and no group declared it, so an operator
# who set `platform_admin` or `disabled` silently kept `open`.
ORGANIZATION_CREATION=
# MODULE_AUTHORITY_ENFORCEMENT: enforce (default, empty) or warn. Under warn
# accounts grants every module what its manifest asks for and logs what the
# envelope would have withheld; the token, workload, build, installation and
# tenant stay enforced. A validation-cell setting, never a production default.
MODULE_AUTHORITY_ENFORCEMENT=
